# v35 native runner preparation notes

Baseline supplied and verified by root: main `c3f18371d120429d10282b24a8e5face4f1937fd`, tree `f4333d6e23702af8bb7b4f37ed9f415063715231`; 734 non-environment blobs. Read AGENTS.md, current continuation/P5 position, lifetime/cutover contract and the complete old runner/test harness before editing.

## Scope and implementation

Owned changes: existing `scripts/conversation-eval/p5-sql/run-local.py`; new `test_runner_v2.py`; new `cutover-native-bridge.ts`; new `docs/pilot/conversation/p5-v2-native-acceptance-preparation-2026-11-06.md`. The SQL agent owns new `v2_concurrency.py` and its sequential local fixture smoke. No application source, SQL draft/migration, preflight inventory/evaluator, old `test_runner.py`, old concurrency modules, dependency, application deadline, runtime route, account or setting was changed by this work.

The explicit --v2 option implies capacity and requires its paired absolute existing --v2-runtime Bun executable. Default and --capacity paths do not require/read/run any v2 source or runtime. All old safeguards and 12+9 case paths remain: nonroot refusal, fresh owned cluster, private Unix socket/no TCP, fixed fixture identity, clean child environment, bounded children and stop confirmation before deletion. No external DSN/host/socket selection was added. Missing sources/runtime and malformed literal inventories fail before cluster creation.

The v2 path installs exactly four preserved legacy read/session drafts and seven completed v2 drafts after the original rollback suites, then checks all 22 exact table names are empty before committing races. It runs the unchanged legacy 12+9 cases first and the new 16 cases afterward; only the last two new cases change fixture privileges. Source hashes include all installation sources, new native module, preserved driver chain, existing catalog preflight, bridge and explicit runtime binary. The child's five source hashes and runtime path/hash/name/version must match captured preflight provenance.

The validator requires all 16 exact ordered case names and successful checks/cleanup, explicit protocol 2/inventory version 1/nondeployable status, distinct observer/worker PIDs, observed holder/blocker identities, committed before/after state, immutable stage-specific ownership/proof/marker evidence, and all 18 prior P5 accounting tables retained with a source report hash. Issuance cases have no later proof; proof cases require the original claim proof; marker/close cases require the original inspect proof and full marker request. The two old-protocol cutover cases explicitly retain parentVersion:null with no manufactured v2 proof/marker. Their exact event sequences distinguish a running call surviving EXECUTE revoke from actual tracked-worker completion/commit and idle/no-transaction/no-lock drain before the candidate. This remains a known-fixture worker-set demonstration, not deployed-host quiescence.

The result separates nativeV2PhaseAttempted (set before invoking the child) from nativeV2EvidenceAccepted (set only after complete report/provenance validation). Partial/failed work can therefore be attempted without accepted evidence. No false unrun inference from a failed acceptance flag is needed. Process-double reports remain explicitly synthetic.

The tiny TS bridge reuses the unchanged manifest/query/evaluator through bounded JSON stdin/stdout, with generic non-echoing errors. It has no SQL client, connection, environment credential lookup, network or privilege writes. Actual local invocation uses --no-env-file, --no-install, one --config=/owned/empty-bunfig.toml argument, empty owned cwd/config and clean environment with DO_NOT_TRACK=1. Source files are copied into an owned temporary directory for bridge tests; no repository environment file is read. Runtime is explicit, never installed or discovered.

## Tests and initial corrections

Final focused command:

```
BFA_P5_BUN_EXECUTABLE=/workspace/scratch/205dbad31641/p5-rpc-work/test-tools/node_modules/@oven/bun-linux-x64/bin/bun python3 -I scripts/conversation-eval/p5-sql/test_runner_v2.py
```

Final result: **25/25 passed, zero skips**, `runner-v2-final.log`: 21 process/evidence guard tests and four actual offline Bun bridge cases. Numerous rejection subcases remain part of those test methods, not extra case totals. The direct new native-child root check uses process/driver doubles and asserts neither connection validation nor session construction happens. No actual PostgreSQL executable was run.

Initial run `runner-v2-initial.log` ran 24 methods: all 20 non-bridge methods passed; the four actual bridge methods failed, with unittest reporting seven assertion failures and two errors across the malformed-input subcases. The actual defect was fixed invocation syntax: Bun interpreted the separated --config/path form as an entry-point path, yielding empty stdout from the empty TOML and allowing a synthetic default bunfig preload in the hostile-configuration control. The one-argument --config=/path form corrected both. The four actual bridge methods then passed in `bridge-config-correction.log`, before the expanded final 25-case run. The TS bridge implementation did not need changes, and no assertion or guard was relaxed. The native module's strict JSON handling rejected the initial empty output; SQL-agent logs retain that initial sequential smoke failure separately.

Source review additionally strengthened the new report validator before final run: stage-specific proof presence, exact protocol/inventory version, retained accounting summary, direct-child nonroot refusal and explicit attempted-versus-accepted phase status. No pre-correction failure run is claimed for those review observations. Initial failed command logs and successful corrections remain saved.

Python compilation passes for the modified runner and new tests. Root separately passed strict standalone TypeScript and scoped ESLint for the unchanged bridge hash (`bridge-typecheck-initial.log`, `bridge-lint-initial.log`). The independent reviewer owns rerunning the unchanged 27 legacy guard tests plus these 25 tests on final frozen sources. SQL-agent sequential smoke reports 306 checks across 14 serial paths and 664 queries, including two expected missing/extra inventory drift denials; root records the final exact serial evidence. Neither test category proves native scheduling.

## Evidence limits and preserved work

All 16 new native cases and all 21 old native cases are **prepared/unrun**: 37 total, zero native attempts. There was no native setup probe, root workaround, network/connected SQL, real Auth/model/voice/device call, paid edit, purchase, activation or publication. The only actual runtime test here was the already installed local Bun bridge; fake PostgreSQL processes exercised harness control flow. PGlite smoke, if cited, is serialized SQL only. The preserved v34 2518/2518 application suite, 822 optional SQL cases and build remain historical evidence rather than being presented as newly rerun for this tooling-only change.

Hosted Auth owner/session/current-policy support and synchronous revocation/current-state serialization, actual deployed quiescence/routes/privileges, native backend acceptance and provider/device finality remain separate unestablished requirements. This preparation does not manufacture those facts or justify another speculative Auth wrapper. Meaningful next acceptance requires a suitable native environment and supported platform facts, without repeated failed setup or Lovable probes.

Narrow official-source checks used for the Bun invocation: https://bun.com/docs/runtime/environment-variables (no-env-file), https://bun.com/docs/runtime (configuration flag), https://bun.com/docs/runtime/bunfig (preloads and telemetry/config behavior). Actual local tests established the precise one-argument syntax used here. No Auth research was repeated.

