The final smoke AST-reads the runner's exact six migration names and eleven additional v2 draft names, asserts their counts and installs admission/capacity plus those drafts in the actual runner order. It runs the exact 22-table empty inventory SQL, with missing/extra-table negative controls, before fixture rows are created. It executes both catalog outcomes through the real existing Bun/TypeScript bridge, exact v2 fixture helpers, fourteen sequential revocation/close ordering paths, explicit receipt consumption/identity checks, all nine legacy permission-denial calls and actual service-session positive cleanup of a retained old claim after candidate revocation.

**The one serial smoke passed with 306 internal fixture assertions, 664 SQL requests and two expected table-inventory errors.** Both PGlite engines closed. These are internal smoke diagnostics, not 306 tests, native races or an addition to the conversation-suite test count. Native cases executed: **zero**.

